// What other modules add to Ordaen Tooltips' tooltips: the contract, imported by type alone
// (`import type { ItemLines, Line } from "OrdaenTooltips"`). Each section is a registry of Tooltips' root (`worth`,
// `uses`, `held` for an item, `gives` for a world object, `creatures` for a creature, drawn among its quest rows), added to in a watch that follows that root; Tooltips
// draws what was added after its own footer (before the hotkeys), a section after another, each entry's lines
// together. An item's hotkeys take what `keys` gives after their own.

// A line another module adds: a label at the left, a value at the right.
public struct Line {
  public mut left: string
  public mut right: string | nil = nil
  public mut color: color | nil = nil
  public mut rightColor: color | nil = nil
  public mut indent: boolean = false
  // What its label opens once the tooltip is locked and the cursor comes onto it: a list of its own.
  public mut opens: Listing | nil = nil
}

// A list a line opens, drawn as a tooltip beside it: its title, its rows, and the notes under them.
public struct Listing {
  public mut name: string
  public mut rows: array<Listed>
  public mut foot: array<Line> = []
}

// A row of a list: a name with its value at the right; it may open an item's own tooltip (a recipe's product).
public struct Listed {
  public mut left: string
  public mut right: string | nil = nil
  public mut color: color | nil = nil
  public mut item: integer | nil = nil
}

// What a module adds to an item's tooltip. Asked each time an item is shown (the same item shown again after the
// game's tooltip went is a show of its own: what the entry reads unfollowed, an age by the clock, is read anew), and
// again when something it read changes; not while the item stays shown, however often the game fills its tooltip
// anew. Budget: one map read where nothing changed. The lines it gives are drawn as they are.
public trait ItemLines {
  public lines(item: integer, link: string): array<Line>
}

// What a module adds to an item tooltip's hotkeys («Alt+Left-click: protect the slot from sorting»): drawn after the
// tooltip's own, as they are. Budget as for `ItemLines`.
public trait ItemKeys {
  public keys(item: integer, link: string): array<string>
}

// An objective of a quest of the player's that a creature serves (it drops an item the quest asks for): the quest by
// its number and its title, the objective's text without its count, the count, and whether it is done.
public struct Wanted {
  public mut quest: integer
  public mut title: string
  public mut objective: string
  public mut have: integer
  public mut need: integer
  public mut done: boolean
}

// A quest a creature gives the player now, or takes back from them (`turnIn`: one of the log's, done): its title and
// its level.
public struct Offered {
  public mut title: string
  public mut level: integer
  public mut turnIn: boolean
}

// What a module says of a creature's quests, by the creature's number (`Game.UnitInfo.creature`): the objectives it
// serves, drawn among the game's own quest rows as they are (under the quest's title where the game's rows name it,
// an objective they already have left out), and the quests it gives or takes, before them while the NPCs' «Quests»
// setting is on. Budget as for `ItemLines`.
public trait CreatureQuests {
  public wants(creature: integer): array<Wanted>
  public offers(creature: integer): array<Offered>
}

// What a module adds to a world object's tooltip (a vein, a herb, a chest), by the object's name. Budget as for
// `ItemLines`.
public trait ObjectLines {
  public lines(name: string): array<Line>
}
